nodes.body:
Good catch. Confirmed: `Image.open(gif).convert("RGB")` keeps the transparent palette color in `info["transparency"]`, and with the first commit an opaque pixel of the same color came out white.

90809bce4 restores the same-mode return in `convert_image_mode` and applies the tRNS color key only in `ImageMediaIO.load_bytes`, for images vLLM decodes itself. `test_rgb_converted_from_palette_is_unchanged` covers the in-memory case, and the processor-cache hash test now also runs with an RGB tRNS PNG.

@DarkLight1337 this changes the fix after your approval, so you may want to take another look.

